    "Always retain a rectangular window footprint and a continuous rectangular outer frame. Articulate the inner chassis with a few shallow side recesses, stepped shoulders and chamfered notches; use darker colors to suggest holes inside the frame. Use horizontal, vertical and diagonal straight segments only, preserving clear controls and exact symmetry or deliberate asymmetry.",
    "Audio level meters and fader fills must be continuous and fully opaque for clear reading; decorative block segmentation is excluded. Discrete segments are allowed only when they convey actual stepped information."
